@startuml US010_SD
title Copying a historical meal into today's log
autonumber
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false

actor User
participant Frontend as UI
participant ":JWT Authentication Filter" as Auth
participant ":DailyLogController" as Ctrl
participant ":DailyLogApplicationService" as Svc
participant ":DailyLogRepository" as Repo
participant "sourceLog:DailyLog" as SourceLog
participant "sourceMeal:Meal" as SourceMeal
participant "todayLog:DailyLog" as TodayLog
participant "destinationMeal:Meal" as DestinationMeal
participant ":MealItemFactory" as Factory
participant ":DailyLogMapper" as Mapper

note over User, UI
  Uses US005 behaviour to access previous logs.
end note
User -> UI : selects a nonempty historical meal and today's destination meal type
UI -> Auth : POST /api/daily-log/today/meal-copies\n{sourceDate, sourceMealType, destinationMealType}\nAuthorization: Bearer <access-token>
activate Auth
Auth -> Ctrl : authenticated userId and CopyMealRequestDTO
activate Ctrl
deactivate Auth
Ctrl -> Svc : copyMeal(userId, requestDTO)
activate Svc

note right of Svc
  Runs in one transaction.
  Uses the configured clock to determine today.
  Validates sourceDate is in the past and within US005's history window.
end note
Svc -> Repo : findByUserIdAndDate(userId, sourceDate)
Repo --> Svc : sourceLog
Svc -> SourceLog : getMealByType(sourceMealType)
SourceLog --> Svc : selected nonempty sourceMeal
Svc -> SourceMeal : getItems()
SourceMeal --> Svc : recorded source items

Svc -> Repo : findByUserIdAndDate(userId, today)
Repo --> Svc : existing todayLog
note over Svc, TodayLog
  If today's log does not exist, reuse US004's first-log creation
  behaviour with DailyLogFactory and current nutritional targets.
  An existing log retains its target snapshot.
end note

loop Each item in the selected source meal
    Svc -> Factory : copy(sourceItem)
    activate Factory
    note right of Factory : Create copied versions of the Value objects and entities
    Factory --> Svc : copiedItem
    deactivate Factory
    Svc -> Svc : collect copiedItem
end

note over SourceLog, Factory
  The historical aggregate remains unchanged.
  Copy stored values only; no catalog or recipe-definition lookup.
end note

Svc -> TodayLog : addMealItems(destinationMealType, copiedItems)
activate TodayLog
TodayLog -> TodayLog : findMealByType(destinationMealType)
note over TodayLog, DestinationMeal
  Reuse the existing destination grouping when present.
  Otherwise create one using existing meal-addition behaviour.
  Each type, including Snacks, has one grouping per daily log.
end note
loop Each copied item
    TodayLog -> DestinationMeal : addItem(copiedItem)
    DestinationMeal --> TodayLog : appended alongside existing items
end
TodayLog --> Svc : all copied items added
deactivate TodayLog

note over Svc : Recalculate nutrition summary using existing US004 behaviour.
Svc -> Repo : save(todayLog)
Repo --> Svc : saved DailyLog with new item identities
Svc -> Mapper : toResponseDTO(savedLog, summary)
Mapper --> Svc : DailyLogResponseDTO
Svc --> Ctrl : DailyLogResponseDTO
deactivate Svc
note over Ctrl, Repo : Transaction commits before the successful HTTP response.
Ctrl --> UI : 200 OK + DailyLogResponseDTO
deactivate Ctrl
UI --> User : confirms the copy and displays today's updated meals and nutrition

@enduml
